{"type":"plan","title":"The Mended Kite","logline":"A gust tears a child's kite; a grandfather's sailor's seam and a gold star mend it for a soaring reunion at dusk.","shots":[{"index":1,"shotType":"Wide shot","description":"Dawn light paints the Brighton pier gold; Maya stands on the shingle beach, holding the string of her red kite which billows high above the railings.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"On a windy autumn morning in Brighton, eight-year-old Maya flies her red kite above the pier.","cites":[]},{"index":2,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"A sudden gust slams the kite into the wooden railings; the red sail rips from corner to corner, a flap fluttering in the wind.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"A gust slams it into the pier railings, and the red sail tears from corner to corner.","cites":[]},{"index":3,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Maya sprints along the wet shingle, the torn kite clutched to her chest, sea spray catching the morning light.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs home along the seafront, the broken kite hugged to her chest.","cites":[]},{"index":4,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Morning light streams through lace curtains onto the wooden table; Grandfather lowers his newspaper, eyes widening as Maya bursts in.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Her grandfather, who mended sails when he was young, looks up from his newspaper.","cites":[]},{"index":5,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"On the table the kite lies flat, its torn sail exposed; Grandfather threads a needle with sailcloth thread, poised to stitch.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At the kitchen table he lays the kite flat and threads a needle with sailcloth thread.","cites":[]},{"index":6,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Grandfather demonstrates a sailor's seam, needle pulling the white patch tight; Maya watches intently from the side.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Stitch by stitch, he shows Maya how a sailor's seam holds against the wind.","cites":[]},{"index":7,"shotType":"Close-up","description":"Maya dabs a brush in gold paint, pressing a bright star onto the fresh patch; the star glints in the window light.","mode":"still","dialogue":"Maya paints a small gold star over the patch, so the kite will remember.","cites":[]},{"index":8,"shotType":"Pan","description":"Afternoon sun brightens the sea; Grandfather and Maya stroll side by side along the sand, the starred kite tucked under his arm.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"In the afternoon they walk back to the beach together, the kite under Grandfather's arm.","cites":[]},{"index":9,"shotType":"Low angle","description":"Maya darts into the wind, the kite surging higher than ever, its red diamond cutting the bright sky.","mode":"motion","dialogue":"Maya runs into the wind, and the kite climbs higher than ever over the waves.","cites":[]},{"index":10,"shotType":"Medium shot","description":"Maya extends the string toward Grandfather; he catches it, head thrown back in boyish laughter, the kite dancing above.","mode":"still","dialogue":"She hands the string to her grandfather, and he laughs like a boy.","cites":[]},{"index":11,"shotType":"Slow zoom-in","description":"Golden dusk bathes the beach; Maya and Grandfather walk home along the sand, the mended kite resting on Maya's shoulder, its gold star winking.","mode":"still","dialogue":"At golden dusk they walk home along the sand, the mended kite on Maya's shoulder.","cites":[]}]}
